  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 235 PM MDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nOn Sunday an upper level system makes its way into the PNW. Guidance \nis showing the potential for storms with this return flow ahead of \nthe upper level system's passage. The main risk area for these \nstorms is east of I-25. Sunday night into Monday morning shows a \ncold front passing over the CWA. After this front moves out, a ridge \nstarts to build, bringing cooler temperatures and dryer air. Some \nstorm and shower activity is possible Tuesday evening with return \nflow. A shortwave passes through on Thursday evening, allowing the \nridge to continue to build. 700mb temperatures are in the 10-15C \nrange in this long term period. Temperatures start to cool off and \nfeel more like fall as the week progresses.",
